## Marker expression over the projection

The expression of each canonical cycling gene is shown relative to its own 98th percentile among expressing cells (colours are only comparable within a gene, not between genes). The facet title reports the number of cells with expression above zero.

```{r spatial_expression, fig.height=8, fig.width=10}
plot_cell_cycle_spatial_expression(report_data)
```

## Sample-level diagnostics {.tabset}

Each tab shows one sample. The left panel shows the tricycle projection for only the cells in that sample; point size reflects the same density-based weighting used to estimate the origin, so sparser (more likely cycling) cells are drawn larger, while cells in the dense non-cycling blob are drawn smaller. The right panel shows the density distribution of theta that can help estimate where in the cell cycle most of the cells in a sample fall.

```{r sample_diagnostics, fig.height=5, fig.width=10, results='asis'}
render_cell_cycle_sample_diagnostics(report_data)
```

## Approximate phase percentages by sample {.tabset}

For each sample, the table and plots show the percentage of cells in each actively cycling phase (G1/S, S, G2/M); G1/G0 is excluded since it otherwise dominates the rest.

```{r setup_phase_plot_size, include = FALSE}
phase_summary  = make_cell_cycle_phase_summary(report_data)
bar_h          = 0.4
max_phase_h    = 12
phase_h        = min((phase_summary$n_samples + 1) * bar_h, max_phase_h)
```

```{r phase_table}
knitr::kable(phase_summary$table, digits = 1,
  caption = 'Approximate non-G1/G0 phase percentages')
```

```{r phase_proportions, fig.height=phase_h, fig.width=6, results='asis'}
cat("### Absolute\n\n")
print(phase_summary$plot)
cat("\n\n### Percent\n\n")
print(phase_summary$plot_relative)
cat("\n\n")
```


